# The materialized RED (D24: sh:conforms true alone is vacuous — a positive AND a failing negative
# per shape).
# =====================================================================================
# A SECOND gate:clause:specification record whose clause:identifier COLLIDES with the committed V0
# turtle-parse clause (gates/gates.ttl gdata:clause:identifier "algebra:clause:V0:turtle:parse" —
# the SINGLE injected violation). Merged onto the algebra data graph the graph MUST NOT conform:
# ClauseIdentityShape's sh:select (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl) returns both this node and the real V0
# clause sharing one clause:identifier, so it flips conforms True->False — the reference
# clause-identity twin tooth biting (consolidated.shacl.ttl:1301-1311 'clauseIdentifier must
# identify at most one GateClauseSpecification'). It carries only its type + colliding identifier.
#
# Depth-gate compliance: the subject is an owl:NamedIndividual with a SPECIFIC type
# (core:entity:structure:class:gate:clause:specification), never an owl:Class.

@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix cls:   <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:core:entity:structure:class:> .
@prefix gdata: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:core:entity:property:data:> .

<urn:silmaril:fixture:algebra:clause:identity:negative>
    a owl:NamedIndividual , cls:gate:clause:specification ;
    gdata:clause:identifier "algebra:clause:V0:turtle:parse" .
    # INJECTED VIOLATION: reuses the committed V0 clause:identifier -> ClauseIdentityShape RED
